row('blend: rect to rect, same corner count, aligned or start-shifted or clockwise, planar sides (parity 40->10, 40x30->10x20 off-centre, 40x10->10x40 aspect swap, grow 10->40, equal-size prism)', 'supported',
  `Round 1: ${rr}. Round 3 start/winding variants of 40x30 -> 20x15 (b listed from each of its 4 corners, CCW and CW, plus the critic's b=[[20,15],[0,15],[0,0],[20,0]]): ${shiftRects.length} cases, OCCT = truck = geometric frustum 14000.0000 in ${shiftRects.filter((x) => x.dTO < 1e-9 && Math.abs(x.occt - 14000) < 1e-6).length} of ${shiftRects.length} (max truck-vs-OCCT ${f(Math.max(...shiftRects.map((x) => x.dTO)))}), faces 6/6. THE PAIRING RULE IS NOT "INDEX SHIFT 0": OCCT and truck both re-align the start corner by geometry; brep-rs pairs strictly by index (see the oracle-reliability row). The supported predicate is therefore geometric and checkable by a student: every side of the first runs the same way as its matching side of the second. GUARD: all ${shiftRects.length} + the 5 round-1 rows pass; guard code none.`);

const n7ref = N7.filter((x) => x.guard); const cls = (x) => (x.truck === undefined ? 'truck built nothing' : x.dTG > 1e-9 || x.dOG > 1e-9 ? 'wrong build' : 'exact');
const n7refBy = (k) => n7ref.filter((x) => cls(x) === k).length;
row('blend: same-count polygons with planar side faces (every pair of corresponding sides parallel, same direction), any start corner, any winding, any offset between the centres, concave allowed (hexagon->hexagon, L->L, tri->tri)', 'supported',
  `FUZZ N7 (seed 4242): ${N7.length} planar-sided pairs (n=3..6, q side i = lambda_i * p side i and closing, concave stars included), q's list rotated by a random start, random clockwise/counter-clockwise lists for p and q, centre offset up to 15, gap 5/20/60. Closed form = divergence-theorem integral of the geometric (parallel) matching; OCCT matches it to ${f(Math.max(...n7pass.map((x) => x.dOG)))} on all ${n7pass.length} guard-passed pairs. Seed 4242: guard passed ${n7pass.length}, max truck-vs-closed ${f(Math.max(...n7pass.map((x) => x.dTG)))}, max truck-vs-OCCT ${f(Math.max(...n7pass.map((x) => x.dTO)))}; refused ${n7ref.length}: crossing ${N7.filter((x) => x.guard === 'crossing').length} (the generator produced a self-crossing outline), start ${N7.filter((x) => x.guard === 'start').length} (truck would re-pair the corners); of those ${n7ref.length}: ${n7refBy('wrong build')} would have been a wrong build, ${n7refBy('truck built nothing')} truck refuses itself, ${n7refBy('exact')} exact anyway. HOLDOUT N7h (seed 99991, ${N7h.length} pairs, run unchanged after the clockwise-list convention was fitted on seed 4242): guard passed ${n7hpass.length}, max truck-vs-closed ${f(Math.max(...n7hpass.map((x) => x.dTG)))}, max OCCT-vs-closed ${f(Math.max(...n7hpass.map((x) => x.dOG)))}; refused ${N7h.length - n7hpass.length} (all start), all ${N7h.filter((x) => x.guard && (x.dTG > 1e-9)).length} of them genuinely wrong builds. FRONT and SIDE planes (N7p2, seed 31337, alternating sketch('front')/sketch('side'), same generator): ${N7p2.length} pairs, guard passed ${N7p2.filter((x) => !x.guard).length}, max truck-vs-closed ${f(Math.max(...N7p2.filter((x) => !x.guard).map((x) => x.dTG)))}, max OCCT-vs-closed ${f(Math.max(...N7p2.filter((x) => !x.guard).map((x) => x.dOG)))}, refused ${N7p2.filter((x) => x.guard).length} (${[...new Set(N7p2.filter((x) => x.guard).map((x) => x.guard))].join('/') || 'none'}). Named: hexagon r20->r8 and concave L->half L pass with dVol <= ${f(Math.max(g1('hexagon-hexagon').dTO, g1('L-shape-L-shape-concave').dTO))}; L -> half L started at each of its 6 corners: OCCT = truck = 7000.0000 (5.8e-15) in 6 of 6; triangle -> half triangle from each of 3 corners: 7000.0000 in 3 of 3 (1.9e-15). brep-rs agrees only for index-aligned lists. The 1e-9 parallel test also refuses pairs nudged by 1e-7 (${J.N7p.filter((x) => x.guard).length} of ${J.N7p.length}; truck error on those up to ${f(Math.max(...J.N7p.map((x) => x.dTG)))}, so refusing them is right, not over-cautious).`);

const cc = J.XA.cc;
